  "title": "Congruent Products of Consecutive Numbers",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "What is the least prime $p$ such that there are integers $a, k_1, k_2, k_3$ with $\\prod_{i=1}^{k_1} (a+i) \\equiv \\prod_{i=1}^{k_2} (a+k_1+i) \\equiv \\prod_{i=1}^{k_3} (a+k_1+k_2+i) \\equiv 1 \\pmod{p}$?",
